---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout mainClasses='page flow'>
  <h1>Patterns</h1>
  <h2>Grid & Flex</h2>
  <p>CSS Grid should be your go-to for common patterns (i.e. the "holy grail", "card", etc.), bespoke layouts (especially those that change based on viewport/container size) or for masonry type wrapping where all child items fall on grid tracks)</p>
  <ul>
    <li>`.holy-grail` creates a grid with `grid-template: auto 1fr auto / auto 1fr auto`</li>
    <li>`.ram` (--min, --max) creates a grid of `grid-template-colums: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(--min, --max))`</li>
    <li>`.pancake` creates a grid with `grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto`
  </ul>
  <p>Flex is useful for single columns or for non-masonry wrapping where wrapped items don't necessarily fall on grid tracks</p>
  <ul>
    <li>`.column` creates a flexbox with direction column</li>
    <li>`.row` create a flexbox with direction row</li>
    <li>`.wrap` allows for flex items to wrap without following a masonry layout</li>
    <li>`.f-1`, `f-a`, `f-00a`, `f-01a`, `f-10a` are shorthands for setting `flex` property on all direct children</li>
  </ul>
  
  <h2>Whitespace</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>`.page[-(inline|block)]` (--fui-spacing-page-size, --fui-spacing-page-inline, --fui-spacing-page-bloc) is used center content that should be an easily readable width (e.g. 40-65ch). The `-(inline|block)` is useful for when you need the appearance of one section bleeding into the next</li>
    <li>`.flow` (--fui-spacing-flow) is used to provide whitespace between child</li>
    <li>`.(start|center|end)[-(start|center|end)]` (e.g. `.center` or `.start-end`) creates a grid and places items in the sepcific inline and block positions, respectively</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Margins and Padding</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>`.p[(i|is|ie|b|bs|be)][-responsive]` (e.g. `.p`, `.pbs`, `.pi-responsive`) sets the padding for the various logical positions or their shorthands. The `-responsive` (--fui-spacing-(inline|block)-min, --fui-spacing-(inline|block), --fui-spacing-(inline|block)-max) sets the values using `clamp`</li>
    <li>`.m[(i|is|ie|b|bs|be)][-responsive]` is the same as above but for margin</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Media & Container Queries</h2>
  <p>There are some default breakpoints set at 320px (--mobile-portrait), 480px (--mobile-landscape), 768px (--tablet-portrait), 1200px (--tablet-landscape), 1440px (--desktop-potrait), and 1600px (--desktop-landscape)</p>
  <p>These are set with custom media properties in the source, however as this is still in draft their value is injected during build and is not customizable at runtime</p>
  <ul>
    <li>`.`</li>
  </ul>

